    // --- Legacy Staff/Sceptre kit. Wired directly into Tool(Staff)/
    // Tool(Sceptre) in ability_set_manifest.ron rather than the pool, so
    // these are cataloged ONLY to run the per-spell `classes` filter at cast
    // time (see SpellCompendium::allows's `by_ability` keying) -- the equip
    // gate on the standard ItemDefs (requirements.classes) already covers
    // that, but modular/crafted staves and sceptres carry no equip gate
    // (Item::requirements() returns None for ItemBase::Modular), so this
    // closes that gap independent of which implement resolved the ability.
    // pool_eligible: false on every entry below: without it, every class
    // listed here would ALSO gain the ability as a free weaponless innate
    // spell via AbilityPool::for_character, which is not the intent -- see
    // SpellDef::pool_eligible's own doc comment. Classes mirror the
    // class_proficiencies.ron Any(Staff)/Any(Sceptre) rosters used for the
    // standard-item equip gate: Staff -> [Mage, Sorcerer, Warlock, Druid],
    // Sceptre -> [Cleric, Druid].
    (
        id: "legacy.staff.firebomb",
        name_i18n: "spell-legacy-firebomb",
        level: 0,
        school: Some(Evocation),
        source: Arcane,
        classes: [Mage, Sorcerer, Warlock, Druid],
        cast_time: Action,
